  "sourceFindings": [
    "The exact-anchor branch follows unchanged identity, candidate schema/provenance, current-region equality, retained OCR evidence, corroboration, anchor equality, residual, global fit and observed-price domain validation.",
    "Observed anchor selection uses strict numeric === equality. The existing tolerant samePrice corroboration helper is not used to select placement.",
    "Exact original-row recovery searches reverified matchedGridRows for equality of its forward percent conversion to the reverified anchor y. Undefined or nonfinite row recovery fails closed; there is no nearest-row or epsilon fallback.",
    "Price uniqueness follows the existing strict decreasing verified anchor sequence. Grid-row ambiguity remains terminal in verifyImageAxisWords before placement; an ambiguity close enough to collapse a forward-percent value cannot pass that nearest-row ambiguity check. The row lookup therefore does not introduce arbitrary selection.",
    "Containment compares the recovered original pixel row with the actual plot rectangle. It does not inverse-convert percent for exact-anchor containment, clamp a value or widen the rectangle.",
    "Non-anchor candidates still use the same global linear row function and percent-to-pixel containment path. Out-of-domain prices are rejected before either branch.",
    "Output keeps the original candidate price and UNVERIFIED semantics. Exact interior anchors as well as boundary anchors now use observed rows; all final real-image metrics require fresh observations.",
    "The full production diff changes only the placement selection/row check. The detector, legacy readers, OCR confidence, independent evidence count, 1.5-pixel internal fit bound, one-pixel diagnostic tolerance, scale rules and retry policy are unchanged."
  ],
